rows.12:113f4:
The videotape showed a perfectly ordinary view of the school.
"Huh, just a botched home video."
Thinking that, he was about to pull the tape out and go home when it happened.{p}

rows.12:114a8:
"Huh? That's me on there...
When was this taken?"
Curious, he kept on watching.{p}

rows.12:1156c:
The footage ended there.
(That's weird. I never did anything like this. Maybe it isn't me?)
The date on the footage was tonight, in the middle of the night.{p}

rows.12:117a0:
Then he waited a while for something to happen.
Suddenly, a lukewarm breeze blew past.
"This is kind of creepy."{p}

rows.12:11b50:
I knew it was thoughtless at a time like that, but it was a rather important tape.
They let me into his room, and I searched for it.
My tape didn't have a label on it, so I mostly looked through the tapes without labels.{p}

rows.12:11c98:
"Huh, that's Tokita."
It was a video of Tokita meeting a girl at school.
Led by the girl, he headed for the old school building.{p}

rows.12:11d0c:
When they went into the old school building, the girl suddenly vanished.
The Tokita in the video searched all over the old building.
And then, when he reached a classroom on the second floor...{p}

rows.12:11da8:
The girl was standing there.
She was holding a huge scythe.
And the scythe came swinging down onto his neck.{p}

rows.12:12260:
The next day, he went to the audiovisual room to put that film away for safekeeping.
And there was the film, set up on the editing equipment as if it were saying, 'Please edit me.'
For a while, he couldn't move from that spot.{p}

rows.12:13da0:
But when I looked closely, it was different.
I was wrong to think no one was there.
Right beside the spot where Tokita's body had been, someone was standing there vacantly.{p}

rows.12:14800:
After a while, Arai came back.
Maybe it was just me, but he looked pale.
"Arai, are you all right?"{p}
